{{Wireless adapter |brand=Mitsumi Electric |model=DW092 |revision= |asin= |fcc_date=11/26/2012 |manuf_country= |is_manuf=No |manuf= |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability= |if=module |if_bus_version= |if_connector_type= |form_factor= |vendor_id= |device_id= |id_string= |fcc_id=EW4DW092 |ic_id=4364A-3149EC |chip1_brand=Ralink |chip1_model= |addl_chips= |accessible_UART=No |flags= |ant_conn=none |802dot11_protocols=bgn |txchains=1 |rxchains=1 |sstreams=1 |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} The IC ID is per the initial FCC filing for this module. :[http://www.ic.gc.ca/app/sitt/reltel/srch/nwRdSrch.do?lang=eng The 4634 prefix is '''Nikon''''s]. This may be used in one of their cameras.
{{See also|Mitsumi Electric W092}}
Per the FCC photos... *The chip used is not easily identifiable (it kind of looks like RT5370P, but dunno). *There doesn't appear to be any voltage regulator on-board.
